course: dictionary
lesson: 3593
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. The word field can mean open land, a sports pitch, a subject of study, or the act of catching a ball. Context tells you which meaning is right, so ask yourself: what is the sentence about?
explain: «The lambs ran across the spring field.» Here field means a piece of open land with grass. «The class went on a field trip to study plants.» Here field means a visit outside school to learn about nature.
explain: «She is an expert in the field of medicine.» Here field means an area of study or work. Maths also uses field for a flat shape, like a rectangle, which has a length and a width.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «He fielded the ball» means he caught or stopped it, as in cricket or baseball. If your meaning fits the whole sentence, you have found the right one.
fact: Field has several meanings: open land, a sports pitch, a subject area, and a verb meaning to catch or stop a ball.
fact: «Field» means a big open piece of land, often with grass or crops.
fact: «Field trip» means a visit outside school to learn about things in real life.
fact: In maths, a shaped field has an area, found by length × width, and a perimeter, found by adding up the sides.
fact: «Field» follows the spelling pattern «i before e except after c», which works mainly for the /ee/ sound, as in believe and receive.
exercise: «The farmer ploughed the field before planting wheat.» What does field mean here? | An area of study | A sports pitch with goals | To catch a ball | * Open land with crops
exercise: «The shortstop fielded the ball.» What does fielded mean? | Threw the bat away | Dropped the ball on purpose | * Caught or stopped the ball | Hit the ball very far
exercise: «She is an expert in the field of medicine.» Which meaning fits best? | To catch or stop a ball | Open grass land | A football pitch | * A subject or area of work
test: «The class went on a field trip to the farm to study crops.» What does field trip mean? | A game played on grass | A bus journey to the shops | * A visit outside school to learn | A long walk in the rain
test: A rectangular field is 10 metres long and 5 metres wide. What is its area? | 30 metres | * 50 square metres | 100 metres | 15 metres
exam: Which sentence uses field to mean a place for playing sports? | * «The children played football on the school field.» | «The farmer walked across his field of wheat.» | «She fielded the ball and threw it back.» | «The field of science is full of new discoveries.»
